            <note>It appears that </note>
            <note url="memory.d.3.xml">Memory.D.3*</note>
            <note> was always publisted as a part of Whist.D.5. </note>
            <note> As with </note>
            <note url="whist.d.4.xml">Whist.D.4</note>
            <note>, chapter XV has only the single line, “Contained in the Artificial Memory,” and
                the only chapter in </note>
            <note rend="italic">Memory </note>
            <note>is numbered XV. </note>
            <note rend="paragraph"/>
            <note>Gatherings B and C are the same setting of type as </note>
            <note url="whist.d.4.xml">Whist.D.4</note>
            <note>. Note that the two books have the same catchword anomolies, including those
                mentioned in the note to Whist.D.4.</note>
